    "Three cut types. A removal cut takes a branch back to its parent at the branch collar. A reduction cut shortens a stem back to a lateral large enough to assume the terminal role — at least one third the diameter of the stem removed. A heading cut cuts to a stub, bud or undersized lateral, and outside of specific nursery and pollarding practice it is a defect.",
